  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Training for communal water and habitat management</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This project aims to strengthen rural indigenous community identity and capacity in relation to culture, water, gender and the environment, and that they are able to engage with and have greater dialogue with public and private authorities. This project will support indigenous communities and community leaders in C&#xf3;ndor Ancocahua, Yorohoco, Callaza in the District of Huacullani, Puno in the southern Andes. This is an area affected by mega projects and climate change, with high levels of poverty.

This project marks a new two year funding cycle co-funded with DKA, but is a continuation of PER283.</narrative>
  </description>
